{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3935","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3935","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3935\",\"parent_revision\":\"37fd7d1e148d23e170a1148dc1f6f836b523e3c7768944ac81ff306c17a85cf4\",\"root_revision\":\"37fd7d1e148d23e170a1148dc1f6f836b523e3c7768944ac81ff306c17a85cf4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe redesign deliberately stopped treating the copied corpus as the primary source of rule semantics. It remains reachable as an offline fallback. Wholesale deletion was not proven safe.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDetermine whether the bundled rule-reference corpus provides unique offline/version-sensitive value, then retain, reduce, relocate, or retire it based on evidence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Work\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Ruff: compare installed `ruff rule <CODE>` with bundled guidance for representative configured-version cases.\\n- [ ] MyPy: compare matching-version authoritative documentation with bundled index/vendored offline fallback.\\n- [ ] Bandit: compare current authoritative evidence with bundled offline fallback.\\n- [ ] Include unknown/new rule codes absent from the corpus.\\n- [ ] Verify reference/link closure and executable documentation/configuration examples; include the known Bandit resolver-agent relative-link defect in the evaluation.\\n- [ ] Test offline/unavailable-authoritative-source cases.\\n- [ ] Identify stale/version-mismatched guidance.\\n- [ ] Record whether each corpus family changes correctness, prevents guessing, or only duplicates authoritative output.\\n- [ ] Decide RETAIN / REDUCE / RELOCATE / RETIRE per family.\\n- [ ] If reducing/removing, preserve any demonstrated offline behavior with a smaller explicit carrier.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Definition Of Done\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNo corpus family remains or is deleted merely because of source size. The resulting layout is justified by discriminating task evidence.\\n\\nRelated: #3932.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ba4b7e8ca5c15bdb59e3c2964d0f8d675fc50a9f16979824d1d2c4f48beeee31\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCK4fg\"}"}